' A real, ordinary ArcoBASIC program meant to be compiled BY the Fission
' Compiler Substrate's own native x86-64 backend (fission/amir/lower_x86_64.abas)
' -- see fission/tests/native_programs/hello_native.abas's own header
' comment for the directory convention.
'
' Random.Clone/Random.Destroy. A RANDOM handle in this backend is just a
' raw pointer to a small {state, increment} PCG32 struct (see
' fission/native_runtime/host_bridge.c's own header comment on this
' section), so Clone is a real value-copy of that struct into a fresh
' allocation -- confirmed to reproduce the SAME draw sequence as the
' original from the point of cloning onward, matching the oracle's own
' real `std::make_shared<Pcg32>(*generator)` semantics exactly.
'
' Random.Destroy is a real, disclosed simplification: the oracle
' invalidates the handle so a LATER use throws; this backend has no
' handle-validity tracking at all (matching its own established "never
' frees anything it allocates" discipline elsewhere), so it is a real
' no-op that always reports success -- not exercised here beyond
' confirming the success return value itself.
'
' Expected output verified against legacy `ArcoFission compile-run` on this
' identical source as the equivalence-testing oracle.
r = Random.Create(42)
c = Random.Clone(r)
PRINT Random.Integer(0, 1000000, r)
PRINT Random.Integer(0, 1000000, c)
PRINT Random.Integer(0, 1000000, r)
PRINT Random.Integer(0, 1000000, c)
PRINT Random.Destroy(r)
